1:extends Node3D
2:## N7 / P4. The visitor: the player as a walker between the games of a world. Kernel-owned. P4: he has a BODY: a
3:## kinematic capsule in a physics space that belongs to the world (terrain/world_space.gd, built by the landscape),
4:## so he walks on the terrain, stands on a plot's own ground inside the plot, and stops at fences, trees, rocks, walls
5:## and rails. He is in no pack's physics space and no pack can see him: the packs are untouched.
6:##
7:## Where the SCHEDULER thinks he is stays the world's `player_pos` (the walk script, or WASD when a person walks): a
8:## scripted walk gives the scheduler the scripted position and the body follows it (it cannot pass an obstacle, so it
9:## can fall behind; `max_dev` says how far, and a walk that is meant to pass must be adjusted); when a person walks,
10:## the body decides and `player_pos` is set from it each tick.
11:##
12:##   visitor.setup(at, facing)      after the node is in the tree (the camera becomes its sibling)
13:##   visitor.step(pos, frame)       once per world tick; `pos` is the wanted position (feet, x and z matter)
14:##   visitor.cam                    the chase camera (make it current while nobody is on stage)
15:## At the last tick of a walk one `tl.view/1` line of kind `visitor` is printed: ticks, ticks blocked, largest and final distance
16:## between the body and the scripted position.
