3:##
4:##   ThirdLife.exe [--record=<abs file>]        the village for a person: a window; W A S D walk (he turns toward
5:##                                              where he walks), the mouse looks, Shift runs, Space jumps, C slides
6:##                                              while running, E enters, Q leaves, Esc quits
7:##                                              (kernel/runner/visit.gd; --record writes the visit as tl.input/1)
8:##   ThirdLife.exe --input=<abs file>           a recorded visit again (no device is read)
9:##   ThirdLife.exe -- --site-job=<abs dir>      S2: the village's construction site follows that Foreman job directory
10:##                                              live, as it grows (also with `check`); missing or without job.jsonl:
11:##                                              the exported copy, and a warning
12:##   ... -- check --edits=<abs json file>       S3 (a test instrument): the walk's `edits` ([[tick, file, replacement]],
13:##                                              kernel/world/jobs.gd): a file is copied over another at a world tick
14:##   ThirdLife.exe --headless --fixed-fps 60 -- check --out=<abs file> [--ticks=N] [--games=<dir>]
15:##                                              the scripted tour of the same village without a window; one tl.world/1
16:##                                              line per pack (its state hash) in --out; `export.sh check` compares it
17:##                                              with the same run of the editor binary
18:##   ThirdLife.exe --headless -- probe --out=<abs file>
19:##                                              what works inside an exported build (the table of docs/EXE.md)
20:##   ThirdLife.exe --headless -- tag             prints "[boot] build: <tag>" and ends (every verb prints that line
21:##                                              first; `export.sh check` compares it with the commit just exported)
22:##   The same three from the editor binary: <godot> --path <engine> res://boot/boot.tscn [-- check ...]
23:##
24:## Why not kernel/host/host.gd: its `_ensure_import` looks for the class cache as a file beside `res://` and starts
25:## the executable again with `--import` when it is missing; in an exported build that file is inside the pack file
26:## and the second start would be the game itself. This script starts the same two nodes the host starts
27:## (kernel/world/draw/view.gd for the window, kernel/world/world.gd without one) with the same `start(options)`.
28:##
29:## Games are plain folders in `games/` beside the exe (`--games=<dir>` names another folder; the editor binary
30:## without `--games` uses the engine's own seeds and examples). The walk is `res://boot/village.json`; each plot's
31:## `pack` is a folder name in `games/`. A plot whose folder is missing is left out and said so.
32:##
33:## Environment, for unattended starts (export.sh check): TL_EXE_CAPTURE=<abs png> writes one picture after 120 physics
34:## frames (TL_EXE_CAPTURE_AT=<frame> names another frame); TL_EXE_QUIT_AT=<frame> ends the world cleanly at that
35:## frame; TL_EXE_WINDOW_POS=x,y moves the window; TL_EXE_KEYS="60:+W;400:-W;420:+E;900:+Escape" presses and releases
36:## keys at physics frames (the same Input state a keyboard sets: this is how the keys were tested without a person);
37:## P11: `<frame>:~<dx>,<dy>` moves the mouse by that many pixels (the same event a mouse makes);
38:## TL_EXE_TRACE=<abs file> writes where the visitor is and who is on stage every 30 frames.
39:## P14: the caches a build ships (`cache` beside the exe: rims, far pictures, rig recipes, keyed by each game's
40:## content) are copied into the user's cache on every start when a file is missing there (PlotFile.seed_cache).
41:## TL_EXE_WARM=1 (export.sh, with TL_CACHE_DIR): the window runs the village's scripted tour to its end, unattended,
42:## which fills that cache for the games beside the exe.
43:## Walker-feel T: TL_EXE_FRAMES=<abs dir> (+ TL_EXE_FRAMES_RANGE=a:b, TL_EXE_FRAMES_FULL=1, TL_EXE_SKYMASK=1) writes
44:## every drawn frame for the blink detector; TL_EXE_AA=<spec> overrides the window's antialiasing (EXE_AA).
